Step 0 · Install PLINK 2 and download the data

sh &lt;- function(cmd) cat(system(cmd, intern = TRUE), sep = "\n")
if (!file.exists("plink2")) {
  download.file("https://s3.amazonaws.com/plink2-assets/alpha7/plink2_linux_x86_64_20261015.zip", "plink2.zip", quiet = TRUE); unzip("plink2.zip"); Sys.chmod("plink2", "755")
}
for (f in c("cohort.vcf.gz", "pheno.txt", "discovery.txt", "target.txt"))
  if (!file.exists(f)) download.file(paste0("https://compbio-geb.github.io/DATA405_2026/data/lab3/", f), f, quiet = TRUE)
sh("./plink2 --version")
sh("ls -lh cohort.vcf.gz pheno.txt discovery.txt target.txt")

Step 0 · Install PLINK 2 and download the data
PLINK is one small program; we download it and the four data files (about 9 MB).

import os
if not os.path.exists("plink2"):
    !wget -q https://s3.amazonaws.com/plink2-assets/alpha7/plink2_linux_x86_64_20261015.zip -O plink2.zip && unzip -o -q plink2.zip && chmod +x plink2
for f in ["cohort.vcf.gz", "pheno.txt", "discovery.txt", "target.txt"]:
    if not os.path.exists(f):
        !wget -q https://compbio-geb.github.io/DATA405_2026/data/lab3/{f}
!./plink2 --version
!ls -lh cohort.vcf.gz pheno.txt discovery.txt target.txt
